-- title:
--   Ld Sandwich Line One Point Prefix Outcome Sum Cauchy Schwarz Facts
-- statement:
--   **The adjoint raw estimate assembles all facts needed for the two Cauchy-Schwarz moves.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $S$ be a symmetric successor strategy, let $G^x$ be an indexed slice polynomial family, and let $\gamma,\zeta$ be errors. Fix $i<k$ with $i\ne0$ and assume the adjoint raw-core bound. For a sandwiched-line question $q$ and a completed tuple $g$ of length $i+1$, let $O_i(q,g)$ and $R_i(q,g)$ be the ordered and rotated left-placed half-products. If $C_1$ and $C_2$ are the two complement-weighted operators in the formal facts package, then
--
--   $$
--   \sum_g C_1(q,g)^{\dagger}C_1(q,g)\le I,
--   \qquad
--   \sum_g C_2(q,g)C_2(q,g)^{\dagger}\le I.
--   $$
--
--   The same package records the averaged adjoint qSDD-core bound and identifies the four scalar contractions with the original, intermediate, intermediate, and moved prefix sums used by the two Cauchy-Schwarz estimates.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.ldSandwichLineOnePoint_prefix_outcomeSum_cauchySchwarz_facts`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
